// [BOOL-COMPARE-OPERANDS] A comparison lowers to one machine comparison, so its two
// operands must have one type. Comparing a `bool` with an `int` used to
// compile and answer `false`, and a `string` with an `int` reached code
// generation before anything objected.
fn main() = print("${true < 1} ${"a" == 1} ${[1] == 1}")
